import Foundation

/// One version in What's new.
public struct Release: Sendable, Equatable {
    public let version: String
    public let date: String
    public let items: [String]
}

/// The words of Settings: What's new (every version, newest first) and How it works.
public enum AppText {
    public static let releases: [Release] = [
        Release(version: "1.16.2", date: "5 November 2026", items: [
            "Changed: saving a new machine or exercise now only defines it. You stay on the gym screen and its tile is there; tap it when you want to log a set. Before, Save opened the machine at once, with Set done and \"Exercise done\", even when you only wanted to add it.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.16.1", date: "5 November 2026", items: [
            "Fixed: the Busy pill is back at the bottom right of each machine photo, just above the name band, where you asked for it in 1.13. Version 1.16 had moved it to the top left without asking you. It works as before: tap it to mark the machine busy, tap again to take the mark away.",
            "New: a check that the Busy pill stays at the bottom right, so a later change cannot move it again by accident.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.16", date: "4 November 2026", items: [
            "Changed: the machine tiles on the gym screen. The photo now fills the whole tile (132 points tall instead of 96), and the machine's name and its last time sit on a deep indigo band across the bottom of the photo. Before, the name and last time were written under a smaller photo. A Busy machine's band turns orange and says \"Busy — come back later\". A machine done today gets a thicker indigo edge and keeps its tick at the top right.",
            "Changed: the Busy pill moved from the bottom right to the top left of the photo, because the name band is at the bottom now. It works as before.",
            "Changed: the rest ring on a machine changes colour as the rest runs out — orange while more than half is left, yellow past the middle, green in the last fifth. Before, it was always indigo. The countdown in its middle is bigger (52 instead of 40 points) and the ring a little wider.",
            "New: a gold arrow going up beside a set that beat the same set last time — more weight, or the same weight with more reps (on an exercise without weight: more reps). Warm-ups, time machines and a first time on a machine never get one.",
            "Changed: today's sets on a machine sit on a light indigo wash, each with its tick in a filled indigo circle (amber for a warm-up). Before, a bare tick on the plain card.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.15", date: "4 November 2026", items: [
            "New: the rest on the lock screen. When a rest starts — after Set done at the gym, between sets in a Sets & reps workout, or before an interval round — the countdown also shows on the iPhone's lock screen: a hand-drawn stopwatch, \"Rest · Leg press\", the time counting down, a bar filling up, and what comes next (\"Next: Set 3 · 40 kg × 10\"). You no longer need to unlock the phone to see how long is left.",
            "New: the rest in the Dynamic Island. With another app open (or the home screen), the stopwatch and the countdown sit in the black island at the top of the screen. Touch and hold it to see the machine, the next set and the bar; tap it to go back to the app.",
            "New: when the time is up it says \"Rest over\" and \"Go: Set 3 · 40 kg × 10\" until you open the app. The buzz and \"Rest over\" message from 1.8 stay as before.",
            "New: on the rest card in the app a small line \"Also on your lock screen\" tells you the countdown is out there too. Skip rest, +15 s, the next set or leaving the machine updates or removes it at once.",
            "Gym rests are indigo, workout rests blue — the same colours as in the app. Nothing is sent to Apple Health or the Apple Watch.",
            "If you do not want it: iPhone Settings → Workouts → Live Activities off.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.14", date: "4 November 2026", items: [
            "New: the picture you share of a session now shows the session's first photo, wide, right under the heading — when the session has photos. The pictures of the machines stay as before.",
            "New: Undo Finish. After you tap \"Finish this session\", the \"Session done\" page has an \"Undo Finish\" button beside Done. Tap it and the session goes on as if you had never tapped Finish: the Finish button is back, the day's plan and the Busy marks come back, and the title, notes and photos you typed in stay.",
            "New: delete a session. At the bottom of any earlier session's page (from History or from Earlier visits) there is a red \"Delete this session\" button. It asks first. Then the session and all its sets are gone, and the dark Undo bar at the bottom brings it back for 10 seconds.",
            "Changed: deleting plan templates moved out of Plan today into Settings → Plan templates. There each gym's templates are listed with their machines, and a bin deletes one (Undo for 10 seconds). Plan today now only lets you use a template or save one.",
            "Changed: the History tab has a new hand-drawn icon — bars going up — instead of the heart-rate line, which looked like a pulse measurement rather than history.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.13", date: "4 November 2026", items: [
            "Fixed: the time of a session with time machines. A bike ride of 70 minutes and 50 minutes on the treadmill showed \"77 min\" instead of about 2 hours: a time set is saved when it ends, and the app counted only from the end of the first ride. Now each time set counts from when it began (saved minus its minutes), and a session is never shorter than its minutes on time machines. Sessions already logged are counted again the right way — nothing to retype.",
            "New: photos of a session. On \"Session done\" and on any earlier visit there is a Photos card: Take photo (camera) or Choose from Photos, as many as you like. Tap a photo to see it large; Remove asks first. Session photos are in your backups and in Check my data.",
            "Changed: Plan today, Repeat last visit and Save as template are now three tiles of the same size, each with its hand-drawn mark above its words — before, they were capsules that wrapped unevenly, and Save as template had no mark. Repeat last visit stays full colour. Save as template has a new bookmark mark.",
            "Changed: the Busy pill on each machine photo is smaller and sits at the bottom right of the photo, so it no longer covers the picture. It is still easy to tap.",
            "Changed: a visit with only time machines shows \"On time machines 120 min\" instead of \"Lifted 0 kg\".",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.12", date: "4 November 2026", items: [
            "Fixed: \"Finish this session\" stayed on the gym screen after you had finished and saved the session — and any set you did afterwards was added to the session you had already closed. Now Finish closes the session: the button goes away, and it comes back only when you start a new session.",
            "Fixed: right after Finish, the session now shows straight away under \"Earlier visits\" on the gym screen. Before, the day's session was kept out of that list until the next day.",
            "New: two sessions on one day — for example one in the morning and one in the evening. After Finish the gym screen says \"Session done. Tap a machine to start a second session.\" Tap a machine and the next set starts a new session with its own time, title, notes and share picture. \"Last time\" on a machine then shows the morning's numbers.",
            "Changed: each row under \"Earlier visits\" now shows the time the session started (\"14:20 · 3 machines · 9 sets\"), so two sessions on the same day are easy to tell apart. The newest is at the top.",
            "Changed: the At the gym card on Train says \"Today: 2 sessions · 14 sets\" when you have trained twice that day.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.11.3", date: "4 November 2026", items: [
            "Changed: the heading \"Earlier visits\" on the gym screen now names the gym — for example \"Earlier visits · Basic-Fit\" — so you always know whose visits you are looking at.",
            "Changed: the date at the top of an earlier visit now has the year, and says \"today\" or \"yesterday\" when it is — for example \"Tuesday, 3 November 2026 · yesterday\". Before it was only \"Tuesday 3 November\".",
            "Fixed: tapping a visit under \"Earlier visits\" on the gym screen did nothing — the page never opened. Now it opens the visit, the same page as from History (the same fault was fixed in History in 1.5).",
            "Fixed: a machine tile's \"Last:\" line now only uses sets of the machine's own kind. A machine first logged with weights and later switched to time (like a treadmill) showed \"Last: 20 kg × 10\"; now it shows its last time (\"Last: 25 min · level 8\"), or \"New\" when it has none yet. The same for weights and reps-only exercises.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.11.2", date: "4 November 2026", items: [
            "Fixed: the time of a gym session. Before, it ran from your first set until you tapped \"Finish this session\" — so a Finish tapped at home, or tapped again later, could turn a half-hour session into \"398 min\" (6 hours 38). Now each set remembers when you tapped Set done, and the time runs from the first set to the last set. A Finish tapped within 10 minutes of the last set still counts; a later one does not.",
            "Changed: a session you never finished now shows its time too (first set to last set), instead of a dash.",
            "Changed: older sessions logged before this version have no set times. If one of them claims more than 3 hours, it shows no time (a dash) instead of the wrong number, and it no longer swells the minutes in History and the statistics.",
            "New: set the time of a session yourself. Open an earlier visit (from History or Earlier visits) and tap Time — the tile now has a small pencil. Type the minutes it really took and tap Save; the visit, the share picture, History and the statistics all use your minutes. \"Use the time from my sets\" takes your own number away again. Handy for sessions from before this version whose time came out wrong.",
            "Kept: changing a set afterwards (Fix a set) keeps the time it was done.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.11.1", date: "4 November 2026", items: [
            "New: the picture of a shared visit now shows each machine's photo — a small square beside its name and sets. A machine or exercise without a photo shows its hand-drawn icon instead.",
            "Changed: the photos in the picture are made small first, so a long visit with many machines still turns into a picture straight away and stays light enough to send.",
            "Kept: the picture still has the title or date, the gym, minutes, sets, kilograms lifted, every set (warm-ups marked W) and the new bests, always in the light look.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.11", date: "3 November 2026", items: [
            "New: a colour stripe on the machine tiles. Each machine tile on the gym screen has a thin stripe down its left edge in the colour of its muscle group, so you see at a glance what you are about to train. A machine with no group chosen has no stripe.",
            "New: \"Save as template\" beside \"Repeat last visit\". Repeat last visit plans today like your last visit; now you can also keep that order for good: tap \"Save as template\", type a name (for example \"Leg day\") and it is saved as a plan template for this gym — last visit's machines in their order. Saving with a name that already exists in that gym replaces the old one. You find it under \"Use a template\" in Plan today.",
            "New: warm-up sets. On a machine, a \"Warm-up\" pill sits before Set done. Tap it and the next set you log is a warm-up; it switches itself off after that one set (tap it again for another warm-up). A warm-up shows with a \"W\", stays in the visit and counts as a set in the statistics — but it never counts for New best, for records, for the chart, for \"Last:\" on the machine tile, or for the tips \"more weight\" and \"one more rep\". So a light warm-up can no longer hide your real numbers. A set can also be turned into a warm-up (or back to a normal set) afterwards.",
            "New: supersets. In a machine's settings (the pencil), \"Superset with\" pairs it with another machine of the same gym. Choosing a different machine lets the old partner go; \"None\" takes the pair apart; deleting a machine lets its partner go. On the machine's page a band \"Superset with …\" shows the partner. After Set done, as long as the partner has done fewer sets today, the app takes you straight to the partner with no rest. When both have done the same number of sets the round is over: the normal rest runs, and its Next button goes back to the partner for the next round.",
            "New: find a machine. When a gym has more than 8 machines, a search field \"Find a machine\" appears above them. It finds by the name or by the setting text (for example \"Seat 4\"). With 8 machines or fewer there is no field.",
            "New: muscle balance. In History, a card \"Muscle balance — last 4 weeks\" shows, for each muscle group, four small bars: sets per week, the oldest week on the left, this week on the right, with the total beside them. A group with no sets in the 4 weeks says \"Not trained\", so a neglected group stands out. Machines without a group come last as \"Not chosen\". Sets are counted on the day of the visit.",
            "New: records wall. History → Records shows every machine's best ever on one page, the newest record first: the heaviest weight (with the most reps at that weight), the most reps for exercises without weight, the longest time for time machines — each with the day it was first done. Warm-ups never count.",
            "New: share a visit. On the page of an earlier visit, a share button turns the visit into a neat picture: the title or date, the gym, minutes, sets, kilograms, every machine with its sets, and the new bests. Send it to someone or save it to Photos.",
            "New: search my notes. History → Search my notes: type a word and the app finds every note you wrote on a machine after its sets (shown with its \"next time\"), every visit title and visit note, and every machine's setting text. Newest first; tap one to open that visit.",
            "New: rest per kind of exercise. Settings → Rest times sets the usual rest for heavy machines (2:00), light machines (1:30) and exercises without a machine (1:00), with Cancel and Save. In a weight machine's settings, a \"Heavy machine\" switch says which kind it is. A machine with its own rest keeps it; every other machine uses the usual rest of its kind.",
            "Changed: because of that, exercises without a machine now rest 1:00 instead of 1:30, and heavy machines 2:00, unless you change it in Rest times. A machine whose own rest you set before is not affected.",
            "New: fix a set afterwards — a long-standing wish. Open an earlier visit (from History or from Earlier visits) and tap any set: change the weight, reps or time, mark it as a warm-up, or remove it, with Cancel and Save. A machine left with no sets drops out of the visit, and a visit left with nothing goes too.",
            "Kept: everything you logged before stays as it was — no set is a warm-up, no machine is paired or heavy until you say so. Your backup files from older versions restore as before.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.10", date: "3 November 2026", items: [
            "New: plans as templates. In Plan today, once you have chosen machines, tap \"Save as template…\" and give it a name, like \"Leg day\". Each gym keeps its own templates. Next time, they are listed at the top of Plan today under \"Use a template\": tap one and today's order is filled in — then change it as you like and Save. Saving with a name that already exists in that gym replaces the old template. The small red ✕ beside a template deletes it after a question; today's plan stays.",
            "New: muscle groups are yours. Settings → Muscle groups lists them in your order. Tap one to rename it or pick another of 12 colours; \"Add a muscle group\" makes a new one (for example Glutes); drag the handles to arrange them; delete one after a question — its machines go back to \"Not chosen\" and their sets stay.",
            "Changed: the machine edit page, the statistics in History and the gym visit page use your muscle groups — your names, your colours and your order (when two groups have the same number of sets, your order decides).",
            "Changed: a deleted machine or exercise also drops out of every template; a template left empty is removed.",
            "Kept: machines you gave a muscle group in 1.9 keep it — nothing to do. Time machines without a group still count as Cardio, as long as Cardio exists.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.9.3", date: "3 November 2026", items: [
            "New: drag handles in Plan today. The machines you chose are listed at the top under \"Today's order\", each with a handle on the right — drag it to move the machine up or down. The red minus takes a machine out. Below, under \"Add or take out\", tap a machine to add it at the end. \"Change\" on today's plan opens the same page, so you can adjust the order at any time during the visit.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.9.2", date: "3 November 2026", items: [
            "Fixed: \"Plan today\" opened a machine instead of the plan in a gym whose photos were taken upright (your home gym). An upright photo on a wide tile reached invisibly above the tile and caught the tap meant for Plan today. Photos now take taps only inside their own tile — this also makes \"Repeat last visit\" and the gym menu safe to tap.",
            "Fixed: when the app started without its workouts file (for example after restoring a backup without workouts), it could tidy away the gym's photos before reading the gym log. The gym log is now read first.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.9.1", date: "3 November 2026", items: [
            "Fixed: the Train / History / Settings bar no longer covers the bottom of a page. \"Exercise done\" on a machine was hidden underneath it, and so was the last session in History.",
            "Changed: a gym visit in History is now colourful: the day and gym on an indigo card with tiles for time, sets, kilograms lifted and machines; a New best line; and a card per machine with its muscle group in colour, each set as a small chip, the plan for next time and your note.",
            "Changed: while you type, the keyboard takes the place of the bar at the bottom.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.9", date: "3 November 2026", items: [
            "New: statistics in History. A \"This week | This month\" switch over colourful tiles: sessions, minutes, exercises (one per machine per visit), sets and kilograms lifted.",
            "New: muscle groups. Each machine or exercise can have one — chest, back, shoulders, arms, legs, core or cardio — chosen in its edit page under \"Muscle group\". History shows sets per muscle group as coloured bars. Time machines without a group count as cardio; others show as \"Not chosen\" with a hint.",
            "New: warm-up and cardio in History: minutes on each time machine (treadmill, rower, bike) in the week or month, with small bars.",
            "New: streaks, records and badges. Weeks in a row, your best streak and records this month, and seven badges — First session, 10 sessions, 50 sessions, 4 weeks in a row, 1000 kg in one visit, 100 reps in one week, 60 cardio minutes in one week. Earned badges are in full colour; locked ones say how to get them.",
            "New: \"Exercise done\" — a big pill at the bottom of every machine and exercise. It takes you back to the machines, in place of the back arrow at the top left, which is gone. The green \"Next ›\" beside Set done still goes straight on to the next machine in today's plan.",
            "New: a machine's History at the bottom shows each visit's sets, the plan for next time and your note.",
            "Changed: Cancel and Save are at the bottom of every edit page, for one hand — workouts, machines, sets, next time, notes, plan today, the calendar and the icon picker. Escape is still Cancel on a keyboard.",
            "Changed: the gym screen has a large, bold \"At the gym\" heading, and says \"Tap the machine you'll use next — or plan today's order.\"",
            "Changed: new hand-drawn icons — a gym building for At the gym, a push-up for Push-ups (unless you chose another icon), and a real gear with six teeth for Settings instead of the sun.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.8", date: "3 November 2026", items: [
            "New: a rest alarm that works with the iPhone locked. When a rest ends — at the gym, in a Sets & reps workout, or before an interval round — the phone buzzes and shows \"Rest over\" with what comes next (\"Set 3 on Leg press\"), even with the screen off or another app open. The first time, the iPhone asks whether the app may send notifications: tap Allow. With the app open you hear the app's own sound as before.",
            "New: Undo. After deleting a workout, a machine or exercise, a set, or a session in History, a dark bar at the bottom says what was deleted, with an Undo button, for 10 seconds. Undo puts everything back, photos included.",
            "New: a backup reminder. When there has been no backup for 2 weeks (Back up now or the automatic backup), a note at the top of Train says so, with \"Back up\" (opens Backups) and \"Later\" (quiet for 3 days).",
            "New: the week picture in History shows 12 weeks instead of 8, with a switch between Sessions and Minutes. This week's bar is in full colour. Tap a bar to see that week's sessions under the chart (\"Week of 26 Oct\"); tap it again to close.",
            "New: Settings → \"Check my data\". It reads all your workouts, the gym log, History and every photo, and says \"All good\" — or lists in red what is wrong: a damaged file, a missing photo, or a file the app kept aside because it could not read it. It only looks; it never changes anything.",
            "Changed: behind the scenes, tests now prove that 2 years of gym visits and a backup with 200 photos stay fast (a backup of that size takes under a second), and the automatic tests on GitHub run again after every change.",
            "Fixed: since 1.6 one automatic test could no longer reach a machine's Weight step setting (the form had grown by the Icon row). Only the test was wrong; the app was fine.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.7", date: "3 November 2026", items: [
            "New: \"Repeat last visit\" on the gym screen, beside \"Plan today\". One tap plans today with the machines and exercises of your last visit to this gym, in the order you used them. Machines deleted since then are left out. It shows only when there is a last visit and no plan yet today; the plan then works as any plan — Later, Skip today, Swap, Remove, Change.",
            "New: automatic backup. Settings → Backups → \"Back up automatically…\" asks once for a folder — best a folder in iCloud Drive. The app saves a backup there straight away, then by itself once a day, when you open the app or leave it. Only the newest 7 of its backups in that folder are kept; other files there are never touched.",
            "New: the Automatic part of Backups shows the folder, when the last automatic backup was made, and a red line if one could not be saved. \"Choose another folder…\" changes the folder; \"Stop automatic backup\" turns it off (the backups already in the folder stay).",
            "Fixed: in 1.6 test builds, a second file picker on the Backups page could stay closed. One picker now serves both \"Restore from a file…\" and choosing the folder.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.6", date: "3 November 2026", items: [
            "New: exercises without a machine. The gym's add tile now says \"New machine or exercise\". Push-ups, sit-ups and pull-ups can be logged in the gym log like any machine, with reps only and no weight.",
            "New: \"Skip photo\". When the camera opens for a new machine, a \"Skip photo\" button goes straight to the form without a photo. The tile then shows the hand-drawn strength mark instead of a picture.",
            "New: \"What you log\" in the machine form has a third choice, \"Reps only\", next to Weight × reps and Time. The form is then headed \"New exercise\" (\"Edit exercise\" when you change one), and the delete button says \"Delete exercise\".",
            "New: a reps-only exercise has its own \"Rest\" setting (none up to 5:00 in 15-second steps, usual 1:30) but no weight step and no \"More weight at\", because there is no weight.",
            "New: a new reps-only exercise starts at 10 reps. On the exercise screen you only set the reps, with − and + (or type the number). The set editor and \"Next time\" ask for reps only too.",
            "New: getting stronger on an exercise. When every set last time reached the first set's reps, it suggests one rep more — for example \"Try 16 reps — every set last time reached 15\".",
            "New: \"New best\" on a reps-only exercise means the most reps in one set. The small chart in History shows reps per visit, and its axis says reps.",
            "New: reps-only exercises are written plainly. A set reads \"12 reps\", an entry \"15, 15, 12 reps\", and the tile on the gym screen shows \"Last: 15 reps\".",
            "New: Plan today, Busy, Next ›, notes, \"Next time\" and the history of earlier visits all work for exercises just as they do for machines.",
            "New: a plank. Choose Time in \"What you log\" and turn \"Has a level\" and \"Has an incline\" off — you log only the minutes.",
            "Changed: a visit with only reps-only exercises no longer shows \"0 kg\". The \"Lifted\" tile and month line in History, the visit page and the Finish summary leave the kilograms out, and \"Lifted in all\" is hidden when nothing was lifted.",
            "New: Settings → Backups. A new row in Settings opens a page for keeping your data safe.",
            "New: \"Back up now\" (a full-colour navy button) makes ONE file, named like \"Workouts backup 2026-11-03 1530.json\", with all your workouts, the gym log, History and every photo. The iPhone's share sheet opens so you can save it to Files, iCloud Drive or send it by AirDrop. A file in iCloud Drive stays safe even if the app is deleted.",
            "New: \"Restore from a file…\" lets you pick a backup file. The app reads it first: a file that is not a Workouts backup, or is damaged, is refused and nothing is changed. Otherwise it shows the date of the backup and what it holds — for example \"3 workouts · 12 machines · 40 gym visits · 25 other sessions · 30 photos\" — and asks before going on.",
            "New: Restore replaces what is on the iPhone with the backup. Before it does, today's data is kept aside in a \"Before restore\" folder inside the app, so a wrong restore can be undone.",
            "New: \"On this iPhone\". Once a week, when the app starts, it keeps a copy of everything by itself. The newest 4 are kept and older ones go. They are listed with their date; tap one to restore it (the same question is asked first). \"Keep a copy now\" makes one at once. These copies go if the app is deleted, so keep one in Files too.",
            "Changed: machines and everything you logged before 1.6 are untouched. Your older data reads exactly as before.",
            "Fixed: each gym keeps its own plan for today. Before, the app kept one plan for all gyms, so planning a second gym wiped the first gym's plan.",
            "New: choose your own icons. On a workout's edit page, tap Icon. Touch and hold the At the gym tile and tap \"Change icon…\". A machine or exercise without a photo has an Icon row in its form. Every picker has a search, Cancel, Save and \"Use the usual icon\".",
            "Changed: \"At the gym\" on the Train tab is one size larger.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.5", date: "3 November 2026", items: [
            "New: three tabs at the bottom of the app, each with a hand-drawn mark — Train, History and Settings. Train keeps its place when you switch between tabs; History and Settings open fresh.",
            "New: the Train tab is headed \"Workout Companion\". The name under the app icon stays \"Workouts\".",
            "New: on Train, At the gym is a wide indigo tile at the top, in full colour. Your workouts are full-colour tiles in two columns, each with its icon, name, a summary and a play mark. Tap a tile to start it, tap the pencil at its top right to edit it, or touch and hold it for Edit, Duplicate and Delete.",
            "New: a dashed \"New workout\" tile after your workouts. The + at the top right still makes a new workout too.",
            "New: \"Log an earlier day…\" in the gym-name menu, for a session you forgot to log. It opens a calendar (Cancel and Done). While an earlier day is chosen, an orange bar says \"Logging for Saturday 31 October\" with \"Back to today\".",
            "New: \"On this machine\" in the machine form (weight machines only) — three settings for each machine. \"Rest after each set\": none up to 5:00 in 15-second steps (usual 1:30). \"Weight step\": 1, 2.5 or 5 kg (usual 2.5). \"More weight at\": 3 to 50 reps (usual 12).",
            "New: the weight step is used by − and + on the machine and in \"Next time\", and by the suggestion of more weight.",
            "New: when every set last time reached the \"More weight at\" number of reps, the machine suggests one step more next time, with two reps fewer — for example \"Try 45 kg — every set last time reached 10 reps\".",
            "New: with the rest set to none, Set done goes straight on to the next set, with no rest ring.",
            "Changed: History is no longer a card among your workouts. It has its own tab.",
            "Changed: Settings is a tab too, so it has no Done button, and the gear at the top left of the home screen is gone.",
            "Changed: the date at the top right of the gym screen is gone. It is always today by itself; use \"Log an earlier day…\" for another day.",
            "Changed: machines you do not change keep the usual 1:30 rest, 2.5 kg step and 12 reps, so everything works as before.",
            "New: on the gym machine screen, from the first set on, a green \"Next ›\" button sits on the same line as \"Set done\" (\"Done\" on a time machine), with the next planned machine's name in small letters under \"Next\". It takes the place of the separate \"Done with this machine\" button under the sets, and does the same job: to the next planned machine, else back to the machines.",
            "New: time machines (treadmill, rowing machine, bike) can say what they have. In the machine's edit page, \"On this machine\" has two switches, \"Has a level\" and \"Has an incline\" (both on as usual). Turn off the level on a treadmill, or the incline on a bike: the machine screen and \"Next time\" then only ask for what the machine has, and the words leave it out — \"25 min · incline 3 %\".",
            "Changed: History is more colourful. The four \"This week\" numbers are full-colour tiles — Sessions plum, Minutes green, Lifted indigo, Weeks in a row orange — and each filter chip has its own colour: All plum, At the gym indigo, and each workout its own colour.",
            "Fixed: tapping a session in History opens it again. In 1.4 it showed an empty page with a yellow warning triangle.",
            "Changed: History and Settings open fresh each time you choose their tab. Train keeps its place, so the gym screen stays where you were.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.4", date: "3 November 2026", items: [
            "New: more than one gym. The gym's name sits at the top of the gym screen — tap it to switch gym, to make a \"New gym…\" or to \"Rename this gym…\". Each gym has its own machines and its own visits. Everything you had before is now in \"My gym\" (you can rename it). The app opens at the gym you used last.",
            "New: Plan today (you do not have to use it). Tap \"Plan today\", tap the machines in the order you want them, then Save. \"Today's plan\" lists them with numbers and shows Up next, Done, Busy or Skipped.",
            "New: touch and hold a planned machine for Later (to the end of the plan), Skip today (and Back in today's plan), Swap for… or Remove from plan. You can still tap any machine whenever you like. A busy machine is passed over, and Finish ends the plan.",
            "New: \"Done with this machine\" under the sets, from the first set on. With a plan it goes straight to the next planned machine (\"Next: Leg press\"); without one it takes you back to the machines.",
            "New: during the rest, once you have done as many sets as last time, a big \"Next machine\" button appears (with the machine's name when there is a plan).",
            "New: machines for time — treadmill, rowing machine, bike. In the machine form, \"What you log\" is Weight × reps or Time. Time logs minutes, level and incline (%), shown like \"25 min · level 8 · incline 2.5 %\". A new time machine starts at 20 min, level 5. There is no rest ring and no New best for time.",
            "New: \"How did it feel? Next time…\" after the first set. Choose next time's weight and reps (or time, level and incline) and write a note. Next time the machine starts with those numbers (\"Your plan from last time: 45 kg × 15\") and shows your note under \"Last time\". Earlier visits show them too.",
            "New: Instructions photo. In the machine form, \"Instructions\" lets you take or choose a photo of the machine's instruction plate. On the machine screen a small \"Instructions\" picture opens it full screen.",
            "New: after Finish (\"Session done\") you can give the visit a title (suggested: \"Tuesday at My gym\") and write notes. They are saved with Done. Earlier visits show the title, and the pencil on a visit changes its title and notes (Cancel and Save).",
            "New: History — a new plum card under At the gym on the home screen. It lists every gym session and every Sets & reps, Interval and Exercise-list workout you did, newest first, finished or ended early (marked \"ended early\").",
            "New: History has filter chips — All, At the gym, and one for each workout. At the top: this week (sessions, minutes, kilograms lifted, weeks in a row), a line for this month, and a bar chart of minutes per week for the last 8 weeks.",
            "New: tap a workout in History to see its details; the pencil changes its title and notes, and \"Delete from History\" removes it after asking. Tap a gym session to open the visit.",
            "Changed: \"Skip\" during a rest now says \"Skip rest\" — at the gym and in Sets & reps and Interval workouts.",
            "Changed: \"Finish\" at the gym now says \"Finish this session\".",
            "Fixed: correcting or removing a set you had already done, and saving a plan, could close the app. They no longer do.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.3", date: "3 November 2026", items: [
            "New: Busy. When someone is on a machine, tap Busy on its photo. The machine turns orange and moves up to a new row, \"Come back to\", at the top of the gym screen — so you remember it once you have done the others.",
            "New: when the machine is free, just tap it. Opening it, or doing a set on it, takes the Busy mark away by itself. A second tap on Busy also takes it away.",
            "New: Finish clears every Busy mark of the day, and a mark left from another day never comes back.",
            "Changed: the machines that are not busy are listed under \"Other machines\" while something is busy; otherwise the gym screen looks as before.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.2", date: "3 November 2026", items: [
            "New: At the gym — the card at the top of Workouts. For a gym where you use machines in whatever order they come free.",
            "New: at a new machine, the camera opens; then you give it a name and, if you like, how it is set up (\"Seat 4, handles 2\"). The date is today by itself; the date at the top changes it.",
            "New: each machine is a photo tile. Tap whichever is free. A tick shows the machines done today; the line under it says how many sets, or the weight last time.",
            "New: on a machine you see its photo (tap to enlarge), its setting, and what you did last time. Weight and reps are filled in from last time, so a set is usually one tap on Set done. − and + change the weight by 2.5 kg and the reps by 1; tap a number to type it. 0 kg means body weight.",
            "New: Set done starts a 1:30 rest with a ring, +15 s and Skip, and a beep and spoken words when the next set starts. Tap a set you did to change or remove it.",
            "New: when every set last time reached 12 reps, the machine suggests 2.5 kg more. A weight heavier than ever before shows New best.",
            "New: every machine keeps its history, with a small chart of your heaviest weight per visit.",
            "New: Finish shows what the visit came to — machines, sets, time, kilograms lifted in all, and the new bests. Earlier visits are listed under the machines.",
            "Changed: Save is now a full-colour button. With no name yet it stays blue and says \"Give it a name first\" instead of being greyed out.",
            "Fixed: two buttons had no name for the app's tests (Cancel on New workout, End workout); now they do.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1", date: "2 November 2026", items: [
            "New: Settings, from the gear at the top left of Workouts — with How it works, What's new and the version number.",
            "New: every icon is hand-drawn, from the shared AMS icon library — a kettlebell for Sets & reps, a stretching figure for Exercise lists, a stopwatch for Interval timers.",
            "New: the marks on the buttons (Done, Skip, Pause, Close, Add, Edit…) are hand-drawn too, from the same shared library.",
            "New: the app icon is a white hand-drawn stopwatch on a calm orange background.",
            "Changed: the colours are the fifteen shared AMS colours, in two rows of eight. A workout that had Light blue or Light yellow now shows orange until you pick again.",
            "Changed: Workouts, New workout and the exercise list are more compact — smaller tiles, less space between rows, standard text sizes.",
            "Changed: a new workout has Cancel as well as Save.",
            "Changed: the name under the app icon is now Workouts. It was Companion, which Apple keeps for one of its own apps.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.0", date: "2 November 2026", items: [
            "The first version: Sets & reps with a rest timer, Exercise lists with a note and a photo per exercise, and Interval timers.",
            "Sound, vibration and spoken words during a workout; the screen stays on.",
            "Three examples to start with: Push-ups, Intervals and Doctor's exercises.",
        ]),
    ]

    public static let howItWorks: [(title: String, text: String)] = [
        ("Workouts", "The app has three tabs at the bottom: Train, History and Settings; each keeps its place when you switch. Train is headed \"Workout Companion\" (the name under the app icon is \"Workouts\"). At the top is the wide indigo At the gym tile. Below it, your workouts are full-colour tiles in two columns. Tap a tile to start it. The pencil at its top right changes it. Touch and hold a tile for Edit, Duplicate or Delete. The dashed \"New workout\" tile and the + at the top right make a new one."),
        ("Sets & reps", "For one exercise in sets, like push-ups 5 × 20. During the workout you see the set and the reps in large numbers. Tap Done after each set; the rest timer starts by itself. +15 s gives more rest, Skip rest ends the rest early. A finished or ended workout goes into History."),
        ("Exercise lists", "For a list of different exercises, like the ones from your doctor. Each exercise has a name, an amount (\"3 × 10\"), a note on how to do it and, if you like, a photo. During the workout, tap an exercise to tick it off; tap the photo to see it large. When every exercise is ticked, the list says Well done."),
        ("Interval timers", "Rounds of work and rest against the clock, after a 5-second Get ready. Pause stops the clock, Skip rest goes straight to the next part. A finished or ended workout goes into History."),
        ("Sounds and words", "At the start of every set, round and rest the iPhone beeps, vibrates and says what comes next. The last three seconds of a countdown tick. The screen stays on while a workout runs, and the sound plays even with the ring/silent switch on."),
        ("At the gym", "The card at the top of Workouts. The gym's name is at the top of the gym screen: tap it to switch gym, make a \"New gym…\" or \"Rename this gym…\". Each gym has its own machines and visits; the app opens at the gym you used last. At each machine: tap \"New machine or exercise\", take a photo (or tap Skip photo if there is nothing to photograph, like push-ups), give it a name and, if you like, how it is set up — \"Seat 4, handles 2\" — then Save. You stay on the gym screen with the new tile there; tap it when you want to log a set. Next time, tap the machine's photo; use the machines in any order, whichever is free. The day is always today by itself. Forgot to log a session? Tap the gym's name, then \"Log an earlier day…\", pick the day in the calendar and tap Done. An orange bar says \"Logging for Saturday 31 October\"; \"Back to today\" returns."),
        ("Plan today", "If you like to know what comes next: tap Plan today, tap the machines in the order you want, then Save. Today's plan shows numbers and Up next, Done, Busy or Skipped. Touch and hold a planned machine for Later, Skip today (and Back in today's plan), Swap for… or Remove from plan. You can still tap any machine you like, busy machines are passed over, and Finish ends the plan."),
        ("Next ›", "From the first set on, a green \"Next ›\" button sits on the same line as Set done (\"Done\" on a time machine), with the next planned machine's name in small letters under it. It takes you straight to that machine; without a plan, or at the end of it, back to the machines. During the rest, once you have done as many sets as last time, a big \"Next machine\" button does the same."),
        ("Busy machines", "Someone on a machine? Tap Busy on its photo. It turns orange and moves to \"Come back to\" at the top, so you do the other machines first and do not forget it. When it is free, tap the machine — the Busy mark goes by itself. Tap Busy again to take the mark away without opening it. Finish clears every Busy mark. The Busy pill sits at the bottom right of the photo, just above the name band, and a busy machine's name band turns orange."),
        ("Logging a set", "On a machine you see what you did last time, and the weight and reps are already filled in from it. Change what is different with − and + (the machine's weight step, usually 2.5 kg, and 1 rep) or tap the number to type it; 0 kg means body weight. Set done saves the set and starts the rest — usually 1:30 (2:00 on a heavy machine, 1:00 on an exercise without a machine — see Rest times), +15 s for more, Skip rest to go on. If the machine's rest is set to none, Set done goes straight on to the next set. Tap a set you did to change or remove it. On the gym screen each machine's photo fills its tile, with its name and last time on a band along the bottom. During the rest the ring goes from orange to yellow to green as the next set comes near. Each set you did today has a tick in a circle; a gold arrow going up means that set beat the same set last time (more weight, or the same weight with more reps)."),
        ("Machines for time", "For a treadmill, rowing machine or bike, choose Time under \"What you log\" in the machine form. You log minutes, level and incline (%) — \"25 min · level 8 · incline 2.5 %\". A new time machine starts at 20 min, level 5. There is no rest ring and no New best for time. In the machine's edit page, \"On this machine\" has the switches \"Has a level\" and \"Has an incline\" (both on as usual): turn one off, say the level on a treadmill or the incline on a bike, and the machine screen and \"Next time\" only ask for what the machine has — \"25 min · incline 3 %\"."),
        ("Exercises without a machine", "Push-ups, sit-ups or pull-ups: tap \"New machine or exercise\", then \"Skip photo\" if you have nothing to photograph (the tile shows the hand-drawn mark). Under \"What you log\" choose \"Reps only\". The form is headed \"New exercise\" and has its own Rest setting, but no weight step. A new exercise starts at 10 reps; you only set the reps. Sets read \"12 reps\", an entry \"15, 15, 12 reps\", and the tile says \"Last: 15 reps\". Plan, Busy, Next ›, notes and Next time work as for machines. A plank: choose Time and turn \"Has a level\" and \"Has an incline\" off. A visit with only exercises like these shows no \"0 kg\"."),
        ("Next time and notes", "After the first set, \"How did it feel? Next time…\" lets you choose next time's weight and reps (or time, level and incline) and write a note. Next time the machine starts with those numbers (\"Your plan from last time: 45 kg × 15\") and shows your note under \"Last time\". Earlier visits show them too."),
        ("Instructions photo", "In the machine form, \"Instructions\" takes or chooses a photo of the machine's instruction plate. On the machine screen a small \"Instructions\" picture opens it full screen."),
        ("Getting stronger", "On an exercise without weight (see Exercises without a machine), when every set last time reached the first set's reps, it suggests one rep more — \"Try 16 reps — every set last time reached 15\" — and New best means the most reps in one set. On a weight machine, when every set last time reached the machine's \"More weight at\" reps (usually 12), the machine suggests one weight step more (usually 2.5 kg) with two reps fewer — \"Try 45 kg — every set last time reached 10 reps\". A weight heavier than you ever did on that machine shows New best. Each machine shows its history and a small chart of your heaviest weight per visit (reps per visit for an exercise). Finish this session shows the whole visit: machines, sets, time, kilograms lifted and the new bests. Then you can give the visit a title (like \"Tuesday at My gym\") and notes, saved with Done; the pencil on an earlier visit changes them. The pencil on a machine changes its photo, name, setting or what it logs, or deletes it with all its sets."),
        ("History", "The History tab. Every gym session and every Sets & reps, Interval and Exercise-list workout, newest first — finished or \"ended early\". Chips filter: All (plum), At the gym (indigo), or one workout in its own colour. At the top: this week as four full-colour tiles — Sessions plum, Minutes green, Lifted indigo, Weeks in a row orange, a line for this month and a bar chart of minutes per week for the last 8 weeks. Tap a workout for its details; the pencil changes its title and notes, and \"Delete from History\" removes it after asking. Tap a gym session to open the visit. History and Settings open fresh each time you choose their tab; Train keeps its place."),
        ("Session time", "A gym session's time runs from your first set to your last set — each set remembers when you tapped Set done; a set on a time machine (bike, treadmill) counts from when it began, its minutes before you saved it, and a session is never shorter than its minutes on time machines. Tap \"Finish this session\" right after your last set and the minutes up to Finish count too (up to 10 minutes after the last set); a Finish tapped later, for example at home, adds nothing. Sessions from before version 1.11.2 have no set times: one that claims more than 3 hours shows a dash instead of a time. Wrong time? Open the visit, tap Time (the tile with the small pencil), type the real minutes and Save — History and the statistics count your number. \"Use the time from my sets\" goes back."),
        ("Earlier visits", "Under the machines on the gym screen, \"Earlier visits · <your gym>\" lists that gym's earlier visits, newest first. Tap one to open it: its date at the top has the year and says \"today\" or \"yesterday\" when it is. Each machine tile shows \"Last:\" — the heaviest weight, the most reps, or the last time on a time machine — counting only sets of the machine's own kind; \"New\" when there are none yet."),
        ("Two sessions in a day", "\"Finish this session\" closes the session: the button goes away and the session moves under \"Earlier visits\" at once, with the time it started. The gym screen then says \"Session done. Tap a machine to start a second session.\" Your next set — later that day, or after a break — starts a new session, with its own time, title and notes; \"Last time\" on each machine shows the earlier session. Until you tap Finish, every set that day goes into the same session. Tapped Finish by mistake? \"Session done\" has an \"Undo Finish\" button beside Done: the session goes on as before — Finish is back, the day's plan and Busy marks come back, and the title, notes and photos you typed in stay."),
        ("Session photos", "On \"Session done\", and on any earlier visit (from History or Earlier visits), the Photos card takes a photo with the camera or chooses one from Photos — as many as you like. Tap a photo to see it large; Remove takes it off the session after asking. Session photos go into your backups."),
        ("Deleting a session", "At the bottom of any earlier session's page (from History or Earlier visits) the red \"Delete this session\" button removes the whole session with all its sets, after asking. Changed your mind? The Undo bar at the bottom brings it back for 10 seconds."),
        ("On this machine", "In the machine form, for weight machines, \"On this machine\" has three settings. Rest after each set: none up to 5:00 in 15-second steps (usual: the rest of its kind, see Rest times). Weight step: 1, 2.5 or 5 kg (usual 2.5); − and + on the machine and in \"Next time\" use it. More weight at: 3 to 50 reps (usual 12). Machines you do not change keep the usual numbers."),
        ("Repeat last visit", "On the gym screen, when there is no plan yet today, \"Repeat last visit\" sits beside \"Plan today\". It plans today with the machines of your last visit to this gym, in the same order. Change it as any plan: touch and hold a machine for Later, Skip today, Swap or Remove, or tap Change. Beside it, \"Save as template\" asks for a name and keeps last visit's machines in their order as a plan template for this gym (the same name replaces the old one); find it under \"Use a template\" in Plan today."),
        ("Automatic backup", "Settings → Backups → \"Back up automatically…\": choose a folder once, best in iCloud Drive. The app saves a backup there at once and then once a day by itself, when you open or leave it. The newest 7 stay. Backups shows the folder and the last time; \"Choose another folder…\" or \"Stop automatic backup\" change it. To restore, use \"Restore from a file…\" and pick one from that folder."),
        ("Backups", "Settings → Backups. \"Back up now\" makes one file (\"Workouts backup 2026-11-03 1530.json\") with your workouts, gym log, History and every photo, and opens the share sheet: save it to Files or iCloud Drive, or AirDrop it. \"Restore from a file…\" lets you pick a backup. The app reads it first — a file that is not a backup, or is damaged, is refused and nothing changes — then shows its date and what it holds (\"3 workouts · 12 machines · 40 gym visits · 25 other sessions · 30 photos\") and asks. Restore replaces what is on the iPhone, after keeping today's data aside in a \"Before restore\" folder in the app. Under \"On this iPhone\", once a week when the app starts it keeps a copy by itself (the newest 4 stay). Tap one to restore it, or tap \"Keep a copy now\". These copies go if the app is deleted, so also keep one in Files."),
        ("Icons", "Every workout, the At the gym tile and each machine or exercise without a photo can have its own hand-drawn icon. Workout: edit page → Icon. At the gym: touch and hold the tile → \"Change icon…\". Machine or exercise: its form → Icon (only while it has no photo). Search by word, tap an icon, then Save; \"Use the usual icon\" goes back."),
        ("Rest on the lock screen", "Every rest — at the gym, in Sets & reps, before an interval round — also shows on the lock screen and, with another app open, in the Dynamic Island at the top: the stopwatch, what you rest from, the countdown, a bar filling up and the next set. When the time is up it says \"Rest over\" and \"Go\" with the next set. Skip rest, +15 s or the next set change it at once; leaving the machine or the workout removes it. The rest card in the app says \"Also on your lock screen\" while it is there. To switch it off: iPhone Settings → Workouts → Live Activities."),
        ("Rest alarm", "When a rest ends, the iPhone buzzes and shows \"Rest over\" with what comes next — also when it is locked or another app is open. Allow notifications when the iPhone asks the first time; if you said no, turn them on in the iPhone's Settings → Notifications → Workouts."),
        ("Undo", "Deleted something by mistake — a workout, a machine or exercise, a set, a whole gym session, a plan template, or a History session? Tap Undo in the dark bar at the bottom within 10 seconds, and everything comes back, photos too."),
        ("Backup reminder and Check my data", "After 2 weeks without a backup, Train shows a note: \"Back up\" opens Backups, \"Later\" waits 3 days. Settings → \"Check my data\" reads everything and says All good, or what is damaged or missing. It never changes anything."),
        ("Week picture", "In History, the bars show the last 12 weeks — switch between Sessions and Minutes. Tap a bar to list that week's sessions."),
        ("Statistics", "History starts with your numbers: switch between This week and This month. Tiles show sessions, minutes, exercises, sets and kilograms. Below: sets per muscle group, minutes on cardio machines, weeks in a row, your best streak, records this month, and badges — tap one to see how to earn it. Give each machine a muscle group in its edit page so the bars are right; the groups themselves are yours to change (see Muscle groups)."),
        ("Muscle groups", "Settings → Muscle groups. Seven come with the app: chest, back, shoulders, arms, legs, core and cardio. Tap one to rename it or choose its colour, \"Add a muscle group\" for a new one, drag the handles to change the order — the machine edit page and History follow that order. Deleting a group asks first; its machines go back to \"Not chosen\" and keep all their sets. A time machine without a group counts as Cardio while Cardio exists."),
        ("Muscle colour on the tiles", "On the gym screen every machine tile has a thin stripe down its left edge in the colour of its muscle group. A machine with no group chosen has no stripe. Choose a machine's group in its settings (the pencil)."),
        ("Warm-up sets", "On a machine, tap the \"Warm-up\" pill before Set done, then log the set: it is marked \"W\". The pill switches itself off after that one set — tap it again for another warm-up. A warm-up stays in the visit and counts as a set in the statistics, but never as a New best, a record, a point on the chart, the \"Last:\" line on the tile, or a reason for \"more weight\" or \"one more rep\". To turn a set into a warm-up (or back), tap the set and use the switch; you can do this afterwards on an earlier visit too (see Fixing a set afterwards)."),
        ("Supersets", "Two machines you do in turn, one set each. In the settings of one machine (the pencil), \"Superset with\" lets you choose a partner from the same gym; \"None\" takes the pair apart. Choosing another machine lets the old partner go, and deleting a machine lets its partner go. A band \"Superset with …\" shows on the machine page. After Set done, the app goes straight to the partner with no rest, as long as the partner has done fewer sets today. When both have done the same number of sets the round is over: the rest runs as usual, and its Next button takes you back to the partner."),
        ("Finding a machine", "When a gym has more than 8 machines, a search field \"Find a machine\" appears above them. Type a part of the name or of the setting text (for example \"Seat 4\") and only matching machines are shown."),
        ("Rest times", "Settings → Rest times. The usual rest after a set depends on the kind: heavy machines (usual 2:00), light machines (1:30) and exercises without a machine (1:00). Change them with Cancel and Save. In the settings of a weight machine (the pencil), the \"Heavy machine\" switch says it is a heavy one. A machine that has its own rest keeps it; any other machine uses the usual rest of its kind."),
        ("Muscle balance and Records", "In History, the card \"Muscle balance — last 4 weeks\" shows for each muscle group four small bars — sets per week, the oldest week on the left, this week on the right — and the total. A group with no sets in 4 weeks says \"Not trained\", so a neglected group stands out; machines with no group come last as \"Not chosen\". History → Records is the records wall: every machine's best ever, newest record first — the heaviest weight (with the most reps at it), the most reps for exercises without weight, the longest time for time machines — with the day it was first done. Warm-ups never count."),
        ("Search my notes", "History → Search my notes. Type a word to find every note you wrote on a machine after its sets (shown with its \"next time\"), every visit title and note, and every machine's setting text. Newest first. Tap a result to open that visit."),
        ("Fixing a set afterwards", "Open an earlier visit — from History or from Earlier visits — and tap any set. You can change its weight, reps or time, mark it as a warm-up (or back), or remove it; Cancel and Save are at the bottom. A machine left with no sets drops out of the visit, and a visit left with nothing goes."),
        ("Sharing a visit", "On the page of an earlier visit, the share button makes a neat picture of it: the title or date, the gym, minutes, sets, kilograms, every machine with its photo (or its icon) and its sets, and the new bests. If the session has photos, its first photo sits wide right under the heading. Send it or save it to Photos."),
        ("Plan templates", "In Plan today, after choosing machines, \"Save as template…\" keeps the order under a name, for this gym only. Next time, tap it under \"Use a template\" at the top of Plan today to fill in today's order, change what you like, then Save. The same name replaces the old template. To delete one, go to Settings → Plan templates: each gym's templates are listed with their machines, and the bin deletes one (Undo for 10 seconds). Plan today itself only uses or saves templates. Machines you delete drop out of templates."),
        ("Exercise done and one-hand buttons", "On a machine, the big \"Exercise done\" pill at the bottom takes you back to the machines; the green \"Next ›\" beside Set done goes on to the next planned machine. Every edit page has Cancel and Save at the bottom, within reach of your thumb."),
        ("Changing today's plan", "Tap Plan today (or Change once there is a plan). Today's order is at the top: drag a machine by its handle to move it, or tap the red minus to take it out. Tap machines below to add them at the end. Save keeps it; Cancel leaves the plan as it was."),
        ("Making a workout", "Give it a name, pick a colour and choose its type. The numbers change with − and +. For an exercise list, Add exercise adds one; its ••• menu moves it up or down or removes it. Add photo takes a picture from your Photos. Nothing is kept until you tap Save; Cancel leaves everything as it was. Save needs a name — without one it tells you so."),
        ("Where things are kept", "Everything stays on this iPhone unless you save a backup file somewhere. The gym log keeps every visit in every gym, and History keeps your workouts, so you can see last time and your progress. Apple Health is not connected."),
    ]
}
